# English language for code and documentation

All source code and documentation in this repository must be written in English.

## Code language

- Write all identifiers in English: variable names, function names, class names, constants, file names, and directory names.
- Write all comments, inline explanations, and TODO/FIXME notes in English.
- Write all user-facing strings that belong to this project's own code in English (unless an i18n/localization workflow explicitly requires otherwise).
- Do not mix other languages into code identifiers or comments.

## Documentation

- Document code clearly and thoroughly in English.
- Prefer meaningful names that reduce the need for comments; add comments where intent, constraints, or non-obvious behavior would otherwise be unclear.
- Document public APIs, classes, functions, and complex logic with concise English descriptions (purpose, parameters, return values, and important side effects when relevant).
- Keep README files, contributor notes, and other project docs in English.
- When changing behavior, update related documentation and comments in the same change.

## Examples

```php
// ✅ Good
/**
 * Build a hierarchical tree from taxonomy terms.
 *
 * @param array<int, WP_Term> $terms Flat list of terms.
 * @return array<string, mixed> Nested tree structure.
 */
function build_taxonomy_tree( array $terms ): array {
	// Skip terms without a valid parent reference.
	...
}

// ❌ Avoid
/**
 * Erstellt einen Baum aus Taxonomie-Terms.
 */
function erstelle_taxonomie_baum( array $terms ): array {
	// Eltern ohne gültige Referenz überspringen.
	...
}
```
